Day 51 /100 of #DrGVishwanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 103: (Binary Tree Zigzag Level Order Traversal)
-Approach :
I used Breadth-First Search (BFS) with a Deque.
A queue/deque is used to process the binary tree level by level.
For the first level, nodes are traversed from left to right.
For the next level, nodes are traversed from right to left.
This direction is alternated after processing every level.
Using a Deque makes it efficient to add and remove nodes from both ends.

-Time Complexity:
O(n)- Every node is visited exactly once.
-Space Complexity:
O(n)-The queue can store nodes from a level of the tree, and the result also stores all nodes.

-Key Learnings
Today's problem helped me strengthen my understanding of:
1) Binary Trees
2) Breadth-First Search (BFS)
3) Level Order Traversal
4) Using a Deque for alternating traversal directions
